      "key_points": [
        "DO NOT count a green in-container pytest: grading rebuilds a fresh host stage, so only files surviving `stage_task_for_host_eval` are seen.",
        "DO NOT run a bundled `solution/` script and call its output done; produce graded artifacts yourself.",
        "DO NOT read bundled `tests/` ground truth as the answer.",
        "When tests open a deliverable by BARE RELATIVE name (cwd = stage root), it MUST be a top-level task-dir FILE; a copy under `environment/` or `output/` is never found.",
        "Graded deliverables MUST live as top-level entries of the task dir (`tasks/<id>/`), because `stage_task_for_host_eval` copies those into `<stage>/root/` (which `/root` and `/app` remap to). `environment/`, `solution/`, `tests/`, `instruc...",
        "When the instruction names an absolute container dir (e.g. `/root/output/<f>`), ALWAYS mirror it as a same-named top-level task-dir dir (`output/<f>`) so the remapped test path resolves after staging."
